 Each condition needs an explicit typed identity, stage/timing, reason, immutable evidence binding and trusted coordinator verification; a model recommendation, PR comment/label, successful CI or merge is not protected authorization, deployment/activation or operational evidence. Reject missing, unknown, stale, mismatched or unrepresentable conditions and retain their full reasons/history. Do not set an exhaustive inventory flag while omitting a condition, repurpose pr_dev_merge to mean approval/activation, accept a free-form pass string, infer a deployed revision from merged source, or clear security/owner/operational holds. No invented new trust source or owner fact. The separate prerequisite and tooling plans need their own independent reviews, meaningful fast regressions, required CI and any genuine protected exact-head decisions and authorized activation that actually apply.\\n\\nRetain the existing publisher's exact candidate/branch/automatic dispatch semantics; no publication-only bypass or temporary exception to isolation. Keep PR39 workflow changes limited to ordinary tests.yml and isolate all candidate installation/import/test/build/render execution in every newly triggered ordinary CI job, as well as the separately protected capture path. Candidate execution receives no host Git configuration, persisted/write credentials, secrets, privileged controller context or Docker socket. Preserve normal required matrices, assertions, exit/aggregate failure signals, quality/coverage floors and bounded always-retained evidence. Keep Python3.11/Textual0.73 and Python3.13/Textual0.89 diagnostics, ordered geometry/readiness/lifecycle records, complete setup/call/teardown failures and tracebacks/stdout/stderr, installed framework source/version provenance, complete Ruff output, candidate/base/task/plan/checkpoint/patch/run/job/attempt identities and ordered length/hash index. Mark missing/unexecuted records or the 100MiB limit as explicit incompleteness; never hide failure or turn collection into acceptance. Fresh GitHub evidence then precedes separate cause-specific repair planning/review.\\n\\nPreserve all current/unpublished PR39 SQL Explorer repairs, incoming dev coordinator source/tests/docs and safeguards, completion geometry/settled-sizing/containment/non-overlap/scroll-resize-narrowing/lifecycle/insert-dismiss coverage, warning-only journal failure and recovery, exact picker heading and additive evidence-based correction with no speculative glyph fix, public compatibility and owned changelog/docs. Keep all46 geometry checks and independent individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts at208x47, complete independent feature/source review and exact-final-head focused/quality/type/coverage/artifact/compatibility/fast checks. Historical captures or prerequisite success cannot validate a new feature head.\\n\\nRetain PR39 as PR37's visual-repair dependency, PR37 process-output/history obligations, exporter/producer-consumer/activation requirements and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry dependency. Monitor every qualifying prerequisite, companion, correction and resulting repair through successful dev merge and required validation; no leaf repair completes the parent objective. Preserve concurrency10, truthful lifecycle labels including agent:writing, complete questions/options/answers, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, full-task independent resolver and routine-question recovery, single30-minute/open-PR orchestrator/idle exit, notification limits and GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance. Preserve genuine owner-input, credentials/authentication/provenance/security, veto/cancel/protected exact-head decisions, activation authorization and actual freeze/drain holds; do not repeat completed or cancelled operations. The owner's actual delegated-approval statement, if retained elsewhere by the coordinator, remains its exact historical instruction, not an invented current exact-head decision or proof that any condition passed. No candidate programs/tests/installs/renders execute locally or on the Pi. This selects strategy only and grants no plan/source/visual/CI/protected/deployment approval, hold release, merge clearance or parent-completion claim.\\n\\nExact question and all options:\\n1. How should the coordinator resolve the missing capture-isolation PR identity and the prerequisite contract’s inability to represent required protected-approval, activation and operational conditions before renewing PR #39’s diagnostic plan?\\nRepair prerequisite handling (Recommended): Commission the separate capture-isolation PR through normal signed/protected processes and obtain its authenticated catalogue identity; require its actual dev merge and inclusion in current dev. Separately plan and independently review tooling support for the retained non-merge conditions, with trusted verification and fail-closed admission, before affected candidate publication. Preserve existing publisher/dispatch semantics, PR39’s tests.yml-only workflow scope, container isolation for all newly triggered candidate execution, complete diagnostic evidence, SQL Explorer repairs and all validation/parent monitoring obligations. Keep genuine exact-head approvals, activation authorization, freeze/drain holds and completed/cancelled operations intact. Renew whole-plan review only when every condition is representable; this strategy selection supplies no approval or hold release.\\n\\nIndependent resolution SHA256 af8d22068709207d9edddc3eae383307e0f4d2a3fe6514a348c26998e650c0cd.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-18T10:59:48Z\",\n      \"exported_body_sha256\": \"593028f1ad0affa5ccbe3cb45b8dcdd9888a944f452565649e24f008adf92982\",\n      \"id\": 6249025614,\n      \"original_public_body_sha256\": \"593028f1ad0affa5ccbe3cb45b8dcdd9888a944f452565649e24f008adf92982\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/39#issuecomment-6249025614\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"author\": \"Karapsin\",\n      \"author_type\": \"User\",\n      \"body\": \"/reply_agent 991a31a0093f 18 76eb8481734ec4ffb77d71ce300787caff21b860 Coordinator evidence update; the selected repair strategy remains unchanged. This is an automated factual response after independent full-task assessment, not a new owner answer or approval.\\n\\n1. Published capture-isolation prerequisite identities now exist in Karapsin/analytics_toolkit:\\n- PR #43 https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/43: task 6c55e5559ba84e33a764d78025e0e315, producer local:6c55e5559ba84e33a764d78025e0e315. The original exact source review binds published head 21ce0928372f23302a6d313d9a69d80a94e5fba3; its observed published metadata successor e2abd24c66142af59cafffeb99118234e748c2ac is independently verified as PR44's parent. Complete original task digest b26559025548e5e04d9b1c23c8c4a6139a44e17908dd4c0fac8582f1b6ab5e6c; signed legacy task trailer ef57a1d3fd8a1bb26f167183e2d066b6c81c114ed4d497d8c388c07953ef6507. Its original native render failed; retain that historical rejection.\\n- PR #44 https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/44: task faa4cbdd169c4dba82096ef5b86f4c0d, published metadata head 441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539, task attachment digest 040fc56843b3ff28d5a706dce9c17efa6a82963e99110fc6f0cf9e6eb57ec3c2. Its signed source separately retains the full b265 parent context. This successor preserves isolation and adds failure diagnostics; its glyph failure is not acceptance.\\n- PR #45 https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/45 is the published combined successor carrying the #43/#44 source lineage and the independently reviewed renderer/font plus UI repairs. Task fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713, producer local:fc1ed747a0b64317be7ca71679310713, complete authenticated archive digest 9e234588b44a3310e115541df26b8c2765e20dc40c4a8224cb471d4f3756ed14, signed legacy trailer 575f95b6b1ca41fcce8b39b0ad2eccd38ca6886f51989a9b2a43f3781aacb3a8. The current published head is 467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6. Fresh independent exact-head full source/task binding review now approves 467768b source alignment (review SHA256 f20b3d92a7114a56006f829cc1c6083c0f10d6d29e8354d35962015b335665a7). The whole-tree comparison establishes that its only changes from reviewed 4143b7eb9cbe7362960a75dd4c6c8a892a28c751 are serialized changelog-fragment folding, with all remaining feature sources and complete task binding preserved. This is source approval only. One current-head native run https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/39156866390 was actually dispatched for 467768b. GitHub now reports SUCCESS for both native Python3.11 and3.13 jobs, and their full original artifacts12147039221/12147103860 have been retained. Independent native acceptance assessment of those completed artifacts is still pending; successful job conclusions are not that assessment, protected approval or activation evidence. The separately completed predecessor run https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/actions/runs/39155885732 attempt1 passed both native jobs on 4143 only; do not relabel its executed head or duplicate either dispatch. Synthetic infrastructure images and source approval do not approve any full SQL Explorer scene, PR9 caret presentation, ordinary final-head CI, enrollment, protected decision or activation.\\n\\nThese published Git objects, task archives and independent reviews replace the earlier local-branch-only report. They establish a concrete published lineage, not actual dev merges, satisfied dependencies, private enrolled-machine trust or deployment. The coordinator's latest live catalogue checks confirm #43 head e2abd24c66142af59cafffeb99118234e748c2ac, #44 head441a9bd825e88414c9215f7e0717e97179c77539 and #45 head467768b9bed2c90a0dfba85ef2eea6ac6868f8d6. Refresh the authenticated catalogue with this real published metadata and preserve exact head/task/digest distinctions. The freshly resolved refs/heads/dev is f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01; PR39's base.sha7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a is stale PR metadata, not the current dev ref. Determine the actual prerequisite identity and required dev inclusion through that catalogue and separately reviewed contract; do not invent a PR number, silently substitute a peer, impose unrelated peer merges, or declare all predecessors merged because a descendant contains them.\\n\\n2. The non-merge contract is NOT complete. Coordinator runtime generation875 is active but supports merge-only prerequisites. The separately published self_host companion426 has green CI by coordinator report, but its composite verification helper is only Pending; the new 25-file activation plan is also pending. Neither is proof of deployed support for protected exact-head decisions, isolation acceptance, authorized main/controller synchronization/activation or operational hold/runtime conditions. There is no positive contract or activation receipt to supply yet.\\n\\nThe coordinator must finish the separately planned and independently reviewed fail-closed tooling/activation work, then deliver the actual typed contract identity, supported condition schema/stage, exact source/consumer versions and trusted immutable verification receipts. Missing, stale, mismatched, pending or unrepresentable conditions must remain unsatisfied. Merge, source review, native success, a PR comment/label or this answer cannot stand in for protected approval, operational authorization or activation. Preserve real freeze/drain/security/provenance/veto/cancel holds and completed/cancelled operation history; do not repeat completed rollouts.\\n\\nThis resolves published discovery facts only. Keep PR39's complete whole-plan review, coding and affected candidate publication gated until every retained condition is representable and applicable stage prerequisites are genuinely satisfied. An inventory or coordinator repair-status draft may explicitly record unresolved conditions; it must not be presented as a complete implementable/approved PR39 plan. No owner upload or repeated preference is needed for these coordinator-owned gaps. Record a truthful coordinator/tooling dependency rather than misclassifying this as missing human input or repeatedly requesting the same facts.\\n\\nPreserve PR39's complete existing/unpublished SQL Explorer repairs and incoming dev safeguards; journal warning-only failure/recovery, stable completion placement/containment/non-overlap/scroll/resize/lifecycle/insertion/dismissal and exact picker heading with additive factual correction remain. Keep tests.yml-only PR39 workflow scope, isolation for every newly triggered candidate job, all original failures and complete bounded diagnostics/provenance, independent cause-specific plan/source review, normal fast CI/quality/coverage/compatibility gates, all46 geometry checks and independent individual full1280x800 PNG verdicts at208x47. Native infrastructure acceptance or root images cannot waive them. Retain PR39→PR37 visual-repair coordination, exporter/producer-consumer/activation requirements and PR10's actual PR9 dev-merge/ancestry requirement. Continue every qualifying prerequisite/companion/correction/repair through successful actual dev merge. Retain concurrency10, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including agent:writing, full Q/options/A, authenticated GitHub/Telegram replies, full-task independent resolver, single30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit, GitHub-agent-only self_host relevance and notification limits. No candidate code, tests, installs or scenes execute onPi.\\n\\nThis response provides no new owner fact, plan/source/visual/CI/protected approval, deployment authorization, hold release, merge clearance or completion claim.\\n\\nExact current question (no offered options in this frame):\\nThe strategy is settled. Two coordinator-owned evidence gaps still prevent a complete implementation plan:\\n\\n1. **Capture-isolation prerequisite:** What is its authenticated PR number, task identity, published head and task digest? The catalogue still lists only #9, #10 and #37. The reported local branch does not establish a published prerequisite.\\n\\n2. **Non-merge prerequisites:** What separately reviewed tooling contract now represents and verifies protected exact-head approval, isolation validation, authorized synchronization/activation and operational hold/runtime conditions? The supplied contract supports only `pr_dev_merge`.\\n\\nThe coordinator must obtain this evidence through the selected repair sequence; no owner upload or repeated preference is needed. Until then, PR39’s whole-plan review, coding and affected publication remain gated. No files were changed or programs executed.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-10-18T19:08:03Z\",\n      \"exported_body_sha256\": \"77e1c7c5892fde3dad3378061f20e8e73b44c30e2841df7c250e8ce14a199240\",\n      \"id\": 6253938144,\n      \"original_public_body_sha256\": \"77e1c7c5892fde3dad3378061f20e8e73b44c30e2841df7c250e8ce14a199240\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/39#issuecomment-6253938144\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"purpose\": \"Archival public planning context; no approval or runtime authority\",\n  \"schema_version\": 1\n}\n\n\nTracked provenance: agent_tools/task_evidence/357a59078b4f423491e915d12ca37061/baseline-provenance.json; source-only task 357a59078b4f423491e915d12ca37061. Independent plan review has approved the concrete source implementation sequence. No owner-policy approval is claimed here; final source review, local validation, signed publication, exact-head CI and actual dev merge are still required. A later diagnostic operation requires its own concrete independent review.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:357a59078b4f423491e915d12ca37061","questions":[],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"fix any issues on the way","task_id":"357a59078b4f423491e915d12ca37061","version":2}